// Badges the maintainer awards by hand. Edit with `npm run badges:editor`
// or by hand, then push: the data-assets workflow checks the file, signs it
// and publishes it, and running apps pick it up within a few hours. Every
// release also has this file built in.
//
// Rules:
// - Badges show in the order listed here, most prestigious first; one-off
//   "custom" awards come after them.
// - Bump "revision" on every change. Apps keep the highest revision they
//   have seen and ignore older copies.
// - Only add someone with their consent: this file is public.
// - "since" and "until" are UTC epoch seconds like the rest of the app (the
//   editor has date pickers). Date strings such as "2026-11-07" also work
//   when typing by hand. "until" is the first moment the badge is no longer
//   shown; leave it out for no end.
// - "icon" must be one of the reserved award icons, "style" one of the
//   colour styles and "animation" one of the animations; see
//   src/domain/badges/globalBadges.ts (the editor lists them).
{
    "revision": 4,
    "badges": [
        {
            "id": "early-supporter",
            "label": "Early Supporter",
            "description": "Supported VRCX-0-Nanashi from early on.",
            "icon": "Sprout",
            "style": "gold",
            "animation": "sparkle shimmer glow"
        },
        {
            "id": "sponsor",
